{"id": "amazon", "name": "Amazon Rainforest", "short": "Amazon", "place": "Brazil, Peru and Colombia", "lat": -3.5, "lon": -62, "side": "l", "blurb": "Canopy fruit, flooded forest, and the jaguar at the top.", "story": "The Amazon is a moist broadleaf rainforest covering most of the Amazon basin of South America: about 6 million square kilometres of forest shared by nine nations. Strangler figs and cecropia feed the canopy, fish such as tambaqui feed in the flooded forest, and jaguars, black caimans, harpy eagles and anacondas sit at the top.", "matters": "The Amazon holds over half of all the rainforest left on Earth. Brazil has 60% of it, Peru 13% and Colombia 10%, and it includes 3,344 indigenous territories, so its future is shared by many countries and peoples.", "tip": {"id": "jaguar", "title": "Start with the jaguar", "text": "The jaguar sits above capybaras, tapirs and sloths. Raise or lower it and see who gains or loses."}, "nodes": [{"id": "brazil", "sp": "bertholletia excelsa", "xh": 0.12}, {"id": "kapok", "sp": "ceiba pentandra", "xh": 0.28}, {"id": "cecropia", "sp": "cecropia spp.", "xh": 0.46}, {"id": "fig", "sp": "ficus spp.", "xh": 0.62}, {"id": "acai", "sp": "euterpe oleracea", "xh": 0.78}, {"id": "floodalg", "sp": "aquatic macrophytes", "xh": 0.94}, {"id": "leafcutter", "sp": "atta cephalotes", "xh": 0.06}, {"id": "sloth", "sp": "bradypus variegatus", "xh": 0.17, "name": "Three-toed sloth", "ic": "grizzly"}, {"id": "howler", "sp": "alouatta spp.", "xh": 0.28}, {"id": "agouti", "sp": "dasyprocta spp.", "xh": 0.4}, {"id": "tapir", "sp": "tapirus terrestris", "xh": 0.52}, {"id": "capybara", "sp": "hydrochoerus hydrochaeris", "xh": 0.64, "ic": "beaver"}, {"id": "macaw", "sp": "ara macao", "xh": 0.75}, {"id": "toucan", "sp": "ramphastos toco", "xh": 0.85}, {"id": "tambaqui", "sp": "colossoma macropomum", "xh": 0.95}, {"id": "ocelot", "sp": "leopardus pardalis", "xh": 0.12}, {"id": "anteater", "sp": "myrmecophaga tridactyla", "xh": 0.27, "ic": "fox"}, {"